> **_COLD OPEN_** <

INT. HOLLOWAY PAPER CO. - BULLPEN - DAY

A drab open-plan office. DANA (30s, relentlessly upbeat) tapes a banner to a cubicle: WELCOME BACK, GARY!

GARY (50s) enters, clutching a box of personal effects.

GARY
Why is there a banner?

DANA
(beaming)
Because you're back!

GARY
I was gone for lunch.

[[Punch up this runner - maybe the banner falls?]]

DANA
It was a *long* lunch.

She checks her watch. Then checks it again.

DANA
(sotto)
Three hours.

SMASH CUT TO:

INT. HOLLOWAY PAPER CO. - BREAK ROOM - CONTINUOUS

ANGLE ON

The microwave. A burrito rotates, slowly, sadly.

> **_END OF COLD OPEN_** <

===

> **_ACT ONE_** <

EXT. HOLLOWAY PAPER CO. - PARKING LOT - MORNING

Dana sprints across the lot, **late** for the first time in her _life_.

DANA (V.O.)
Rule number one of paper sales: never be late.

> **_END OF ACT ONE_** <
